}
```

Rules:
R01 identity: parse; schema_version; artifact_kind == 'class_schema'; class_id in frozen; node_id; owner; epistemic_status present.
R02 class_components: tokens list; family matches; matter_model matches; regularity_token_count matches family (SCC exactly 1, WCC 0); tokens decompose class_id token-wise.
R03 quantifiers: ordered non-empty list of dicts with kind ∈ {forall, exists, exists_unique, not_exists}, binder, domain, domain_id; formal string non-empty and uses binders (contains each binder? or at least one quantifier word); each domain_id resolves in quantifiers.domains with non-vague definition (banned vague words allowed only if the entry has definition_ref or numeric content).
R04 topology: spacetime_dimension == 4; slice_topology declares connected, complete, one-ended, asymptotically flat; conformal_boundary lists I+, I-, i0 with I+ topology 'R x S^2'; forbidden list includes closed/periodic exclusions.
R05 data_class: matter (none/vacuum for VAC classes; scalar for scalar class); cosmological_constant == 0; both constraints by name (hamiltonian, momentum); adm_mass_status; asymptotic_decay numeric rates per derivative order; sobolev_index s and weight delta or explicit smooth-with-decay numeric rates.
R06 regularity: separates data_regularity, solution_regularity, i_plus_regularity, extension_regularity, extension_solution_concept; for SCC extension_regularity == class token; must_not_conflate non-empty list.
R07 genericity: kind in vocab; ambient_space and topology_or_measure named; generic_set set-builder/Baire formula; excluded_set present; transfer_failures non-empty; is_part_of_class is True with statement.
R08 non_vacuity: exists with condition and witness_type.
R09 i_plus: role in vocab; WCC → role == 'conclusion' and completeness definition present; SCC → in_conclusion == False and no completeness assertion inside i_plus.
R10 visibility: WCC → role == 'conclusion' with predicate name, definition, negation_conclusion; SCC → role == 'not_in_conclusion' with reason and explicit statement that visible-singularity falsifier belongs to WCC.
R11 conclusion: conclusion_type == vocab[class]; epistemic_status in vocab; forbidden_strengthenings non-empty; not labelled theorem without artifact_refs.
R12 leakage scan over leakage_scan_blocks (conclusion, visibility, i_plus, falsifier) only: no foreign-family token; no foreign matter/asymptotic token; occurrences inside anti_scope/variants exempt but must be tagged. Block-level scan of specific subtrees.
R13 composite regularity: regex `(C0|C2)\s*(or|and|/)\s*(C0|C2)` anywhere outside explicit forbidden-phrase quotation; mixed tokens in extension_regularity.
R14 falsifier: tier_1 refutes class with genericity/robustness requirement; tier_2 labelled as strengthening; witness_type present; machine_checkable_steps non-empty; SCC tier_1 witness is extension witness (extension_regularity); WCC tier_1 witness is visible incomplete causal geodesic.
R15 provenance: citation_status in vocab; if verified then ≥1 source with identifier and retrieval date; unresolved_citations present; no source presented as establishing the class conclusion (check source_conclusion_disclaimer or absence of overclaim words).
R16 (SCC only): implication_ledger records C2 ⊂ C0 one-way statements and marks converse/WCC↔SCC transfers forbidden_or_unresolved.

Note the revision requirement mentions R04 and R08 as "one-end topology" and "conclusion is the negation of visibility" — but the published spec has R04 topology and R08 non_vacuity; R09/R10 handle I+/visibility; R11 conclusion. The lead's revision text may refer to my old numbering. I'll implement the published spec's R01-R16 and make all family-specific behaviour parameterised. I'll note the mapping in the README (old WP13 R08/R04 → published R11/R10/R09/R04).

